# Prototype Kit Reuse

When designing or implementing an AI-generated prototype:

1. Inspect `specs/components/*.yaml`, matching MDX guidance, and existing `components/kit` implementations before writing UI.
2. Reuse existing Kit components whenever the design contains their responsibility:
   - Tags and badges → `list-tag`
   - Action or message rows → `regular-list`
   - Page title bars and tabs → the matching navigation component
   - Icons → `SystemIcon`, `BottomNavigationIcon`, `SearchControl`, or extend `generate-inline-icon-assets.mjs`; never CSS mask or rasterized SVG `<img>` (see `prototype-asset-pipeline.mdc`)
   - Avatars & prototype photos → `PrototypeAvatarImage` / `AvatarVisual` with @3x bitmaps registered in `generate-prototype-avatar-3x.mjs`
3. Do not recreate Kit markup, tokens, states, or icons with prototype-local CSS, emoji, screenshots, or look-alike elements.
4. Prototype layout may compose and position Kit components, but must not copy their internals.
5. If no Kit component can express a required area, record it as a `kitGap` and isolate only that area as a clearly named `Prototype*` module.
6. Include the component mapping and unresolved `kitGaps` in the prototype handoff.
7. Verify reused components retain their documented accessibility, interaction states, and responsive behavior.
